  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strong: every battery thermal incident must be reported within 24 hours and customers notified within 48 hours, with no phase-in. S2 is weakened by a permanent 7% pass limit (above the 5% benchmark) with no sales-stop consequence, though per-model numeric results do reach customers and regulators while avoiding public disclosure. S3 is weakened because new-unit shut-off begins only at 36 months and the retrofit deadline is 6 years, though a bounded plan is still required. S4 and S5 land in the acceptable band: built-in suppression at 36 months and a mandatory numeric recall trigger at 8/100k with immediate customer notice but no serious-injury clause."
 },
